 "answer": "**I’d have her skip the outdoor walk today, Saturday, October 17.** Singapore’s National Environment Agency forecast the haze at **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy** levels and advises older adults to **minimise outdoor activity**. An indoor walk is the safer choice, especially if she has a heart or lung condition. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))\n\nIt’s already about **12:45 p.m. in Singapore**, so the morning has passed. If she’s considering going out later, check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading for her area** in NEA’s myENV app first; that is the reading NEA recommends for an immediate decision, and conditions can change by the hour. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))",
